# Decided
- Claude: both read "lift … into the DSL": table_reference.h "lift a struct
  mapped as a table or view into the DSL", quoted_expression.h "lift an
  expression into the DSL". Both give something that is no DSL value of its
  own a place in the DSL; "represent" stays with the node Purposes of SQL
  constructs. trueqbit's yes: "yes, commit it".
- quoted_expression.h drops "so that its overloaded operators and member
  notation apply to it": "member notation" points at the members =, in,
  not_in, a detail of the kind da22013e cut; "lift into the DSL" already
  says the DSL's notation applies.
- Re-checked against reviewer checks 3 and 4 after the rewording, as the
  round's Purpose check pass asks: no member or variant named; true of every
  declaration, table_valued_expression included (a mapped virtual table
  lifted with its bound arguments); the shared node Intention holds for both.
